    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d445-a1">

                <pb facs="0610" n="504" xml:id="pg504"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 224.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Black to Mr.
                            Phelps</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Nuremberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-01-27"><hi rendition="#italic">January 27,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 36.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that I
                    received from the colonel of the Fourteenth Regiment here an answer to my
                    request for information as to John Haberacker.</p>
                <p>While the answer is not direct, it, I think, undoubtedly shows that Haberacker is
                    still in the military service here. Independent of that, however, my secretary
                    informs me that when he went to the barracks to deliver my letter thanking the
                    colonel for his information, the “Unterofficier” on duty in the colonel’s office
                    told him that John Haberacker is at present serving in the first company of the
                    Fourteenth Regiment in this city.</p>
                <p>I inclose you my letter to the colonel and his reply to the same, and when you
                    have finished with them you will be kind enough to return them, so that I can
                    place them on file in this consulate.</p>
                <p>Upon this information I telegraphed you this afternoon as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Judge from reply is still here. Have written.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Black.”</hi></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. J. Black</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul</hi>.</signed></closer>



